  "developmentFixes": [
    "The first broad run found the canonical domain SDK version still at 0.6.80 after the package version bump; both now declare 0.6.81.",
    "The periodic sweep overlap test relied on a fixed number of event-loop yields. Adding maintenance exposed that timing assumption. It now waits until scheduled dispatch enters the serialized hook path before releasing the blocked first hook, retaining the original concurrent-work and queue-consumption assertions.",
    "Legacy comments in three touched files were removed to meet the repository strict lint rule; behavior was not changed by comment removal.",
    "A final typecheck invocation used the wrong package filter @bb/plugin-sdk and performed no tasks; the corrected @get-bb/plugin-sdk invocation passed all 15 tasks.",
    "Final formatting found one test-only formatting difference; it was formatted and all 30 changed code files then passed formatting and strict lint.",
    "The first Docker deployment passed live native draining and pause preservation, then found a personal send during simultaneous UID maintenance and server shutdown returned 403 rather than the established 503/server_stopping response. Personal execution now checks global admission after thread visibility and before maintenance dispatch; start checks admission before worker dispatch too. The unchanged deployment assertions and a new migrated-SQLite regression retain foreign-thread privacy and verify no history/queue mutation.",
    "The second Docker deployment retained the established shutdown response, then the old offline orphan fixture correctly hit maintenance admission when calling normal job/thread constructors. The fixture now checks the old server PID has exited and inserts historical orphan rows in one migrated-SQLite transaction. It does not change production guards or move the saved maintenance intent past shutdown.",
    "Automation due-page selection could be filled by 100 paused-owner rows, delaying other owners indefinitely. Paused owner filtering now runs in SQL before pagination; a real plugin-SQLite regression places Bob behind 101 paused Alice schedules and verifies Bob remains selectable without changing Alice cursors.",
    "The third Docker deployment completed saved UID maintenance at startup, then exposed a notification replay bug: private job authority converted temporary maintenance into a generic 403, and notification delivery treated it as permanent denial. The private authority/notification adapters now preserve the typed maintenance fault; builtin Workflows defers paused-owner notifications before beginning an attempt. Current profile revocation still produces permanent denial.",
    "The first notification regression reproduced the lost private reason and failed until job-authority preserved it; the original notification receipt and revocation assertions were retained.",
    "The fourth deployment passed the new lifecycle, startup recovery and notification receipt replay, then exhausted the unchanged 540-second composite budget at final crash-recovery cleanup. The new live-drain scenario now runs in a separate fresh Docker container with a 150-second inner/180-second outer budget. The original full composite matrix retains its 540/570-second budgets and the saved-maintenance-before-shutdown regression. Both Docker suites run sequentially through the same deployment task; neither old assertions nor the crash matrix were removed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Administrative grant changes are not yet atomically combined with participant reservation through a public role API/SDK/CLI/UI.",
    "Actual shared native project execution remains closed.",
    "Unknown native stop completion retains the live worker claim until process exit; no unsafe in-process takeover is attempted.",
    "A changed policy requires explicit rebase; periodic recovery never silently changes the pinned authorization decision.",
    "Interrupted accepted turns are durable interruptions; external side effects are not claimed exactly once.",
    "Native active workflow interruption and shared-project role changes still require composite acceptance beyond queued workflow and due-schedule deferral.",
    "The Docker fixture creates private saved operations, not a user-facing role mutation endpoint.",
    "The maintenance interruption label has unit coverage and App typechecking; a browser check of that specific label was not run."
  ]
